{{Quote|Grand Admiral Ackbar.''"<br />"Grand admiral'' is an Imperial ranking. I, like you once did, identify as ''fleet admiral''&mdash;but you seem to have taken the title 'Grand Admiral' for yourself.|Grand Admiral Rae Sloane and [[Fleet Admiral]] Gial Ackbar|<ref name="Life Debt" />}}
'''Grand Admiral''' was a senior [[military rank]] in the [[Imperial Navy]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. It was also a rank in the [[Mon Cala Mercantile Fleet]]. After the [[Galactic Concordance|downfall]] of the Empire, the rank was active in the [[First Order]], one of its successor states.

==Description==
===Galactic Empire===
====Overview====
The Imperial rank of Grand Admiral was one of the most senior ranks in the entire [[Imperial Military]], and to be given the title was seen as a great honor.<ref name="Life Debt" /> A Grand Admiral was typically given command of a fleet, such as Thrawn with the [[Seventh Fleet (Galactic Empire)|Seventh Fleet]]<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" /> and Savit with the [[Third Fleet]].<ref name="Treason" /> A Grand Admiral also had the authority to issue the status of a most wanted [[bounty]].<ref name="Scum and Villainy">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref> The rank was held by only twelve [[Imperial officer]]s at a time, who were generally recognized as possessing superior skills in tactics and strategy.<ref name="Rise">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

Imperial officers who served as Grand Admirals include:
*'''[[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]]'''&mdash; [[Commander]] of the Imperial [[Seventh Fleet (Galactic Empire)|Seventh Fleet]].<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" />
*'''[[Balanhai Savit]]'''&mdash; Commander of the Imperial [[Third Fleet]].<ref name="Treason" />
*'''[[Rae Sloane]]'''&mdash; Commander of loyalist Imperial forces controlled by the [[Shadow Council]] following the [[death]] of [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]].<ref name="Life Debt" />

====Uniform====
{{Main|Grand Admiral's uniform}}
{{Quote|Even if the locals do not recognize the uniform of an Imperial grand admiral, they will nevertheless recognize that it ''is'' a uniform.|Grand Admiral Thrawn, before landing on [[Batuu]]|<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances">''[[Thrawn: Alliances]]''</ref>}}
Unlike the [[Imperial military uniforms|traditional Imperial uniform]], which generally consisted of a plain gray tunic, the Imperial [[Grand Admiral's uniform|grand admiral's uniform]] was white with golden epaulets.<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" /> Such accessories were generally uncommon in the Imperial Military, as they seemed to put an emphasis on status above duty and humility.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

===Mon Cala===
The [[Mon Calamari monarchy]] also used the rank of Grand Admiral within their structure for the [[Mon Cala Mercantile Fleet]]. The rank could be used concurrently with other titles and positions, including [[Regent]] of [[Mon Cala]], [[Warden]] of the [[King of Mon Cala]], and [[Dual Protector of the Two People]].<ref name="Star Wars 44" />

Mon Calamari individuals who served as Grand Admiral include:
*'''[[Dors Urtya]]'''&mdash; Regent of Mon Cala, who additionally commanded the Mon Calamari Merchant Fleet.<ref name="Star Wars 44" />

==History==
===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Grand Admiral Thrawn.''"''<br />''"''<nowiki />''Grand'' Admiral?''"''<br />''"''The Emperor recently promoted me after my victory at Batonn.|Grand Moff Wilhuff Tarkin, Admiral Kassius Konstantine, and Grand Admiral Thrawn|<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" />}}
[[File:ThrawnPromotion-Thrawn6.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Grand Admiral Mitth'raw'nuruodo "Thrawn" receives his rank from Emperor Palpatine himself.]]
Following the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Imperial Military]] reorganized its branches under the [[New Order]]. At the top of the new fleet structure was the rank of grand admiral.<ref name="Rise" /> Shortly after his victory over the [[Batonn sector insurgency]], [[Chiss]] [[Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] was awarded the rank of Grand Admiral by [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]],<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" /> becoming one of the Empire's twelve Grand Admirals.<ref name="Treason">''[[Thrawn: Treason]]''</ref>

Imperial Grand Admirals occasionally cooperated in strategic concerns, such as Thrawn and [[Balanhai Savit]] concerning delays to [[Project Stardust]]. However, their dealings were often colored by intra-service struggles&mdash;such as Thrawn's advocacy of the [[TIE/d "Defender" Multi-Role Starfighter|TIE Defender program]] and Savit's opposition to, and secret sabotage of, the [[Death Star]]&mdash;and some Imperials, such as [[Brierly Ronan]], considered the Grand Admirals nothing more than political appointees. However, Thrawn himself did not understand nor care about Imperial politics. After Thrawn discovered Savit's sabotage, he offered his fellow Grand Admiral a chance at redemption by helping him [[Skirmish with Grysk warships|battle]] the [[Grysk Hegemony]], but Savit declined.<ref name="Treason" />

Thrawn and [[Thrawn's forces|his forces]] were pulled away from the Empire by the young [[Jedi]] [[Ezra Bridger]], who sacrificed a happy life with his found family by summoning a pod of [[purrgil]], which pulled him, Thrawn, and everyone aboard Thrawn's [[flagship]] ''[[Chimaera]]''<ref name="Family&Farewell">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref> into [[Far galaxy|another galaxy]]. There, Bridger, Thrawn, and Thrawn's forces found themselves exiled on the planet [[Peridea]].<ref name="Part Six" /> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Mon Calamari monarchy]] [[Regent]] [[Dors Urtya]] served as the Grand Admiral of the [[Mon Cala Mercantile Fleet]], which at the time was commandeered by the Galactic Empire.<ref name="Star Wars 44" />

===New Republic Era===
[[File:WoTG-RaeSloane-Stormtroopers.png|thumb|right|250px|Grand Admiral Rae Sloane acted as public leader of the crumbling Empire]]
Following the [[Battle of Endor]], [[Rae Sloane]] served as Grand Admiral and commanded the remnants of the [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="Life Debt" /> [[New Republic]] [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Gial Ackbar]] was considered a Grand Admiral by [[Imperial officer]]s,<ref name="Aftermath" /> although it was not an official rank utilized by the New Republic.<ref name="Life Debt" /> Taking charge of the Emperor's [[Contingency]] to reform the Empire,<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> Sloane continued to posses the rank of Grand Admiral during the time she was part of the [[First Order]].<ref name="Phasma" /> Ultimately, however, a mysterious being known as [[Snoke]],<ref name="TLJ Expanded Edition">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> secretly a puppet of the resurrected Emperor,<ref name="TSWB" /> took control of the First Order instead of Sloane or other expected leaders.<ref name="TLJ Expanded Edition" />

Thrawn, meanwhile, remained stranded in the other galaxy on Peridea, where he discovered the slumbering [[Great Mothers]]. Agreeing to take them and their cargo back to the main galaxy with him, Thrawn entered into an alliance with the Great Mothers,<ref name="Part Eight">{{Ahsoka|Part Eight: The Jedi, the Witch, and the Warlord}}</ref> who reached out to [[Morgan Elsbeth]] and arranged for her arrival with the prototype of the [[hyperspace transport ring]], the ''[[Eye of Sion]]'',<ref name="Part Six" /> which could return Thrawn's forces and the Great Mothers to the galaxy. Thrawn, his forces, and the Great Mothers mounted a successful [[Battle of Peridea|escape from Peridea]].<ref name="Part Eight" /> Thrawn's return promised to galvanize the galaxy's [[Imperial Remnants]]. At that time, Thrawn was thought to be the last surviving Grand Admiral.<ref name="Part One">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:GAThrawn-SWI66.png|thumb|right|150px|Grand Admiral Thrawn in the Legends continuity]]
[[Timothy Zahn]], author of the [[1991]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] novel ''[[Heir to the Empire]]'', introduced the rank of "Grand Admiral" for the villain of that novel, [[Grand Admiral/Legends|Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo/Legends|Thrawn]].<ref name="HttE">''[[Heir to the Empire]]''</ref> Zahn wanted Thrawn to be a military leader rather than a [[Politics|political]] title-holder or [[Dark side adept/Legends|darksider]], but felt a normal [[Admiral/Legends|Admiral]] would be too mundane. He therefore decided to use the title "Grand Admiral," which he had encountered while reading [[Wikipedia:William L. Shirer|William L. Shirer's]] [[Wikipedia:The Rise and Fall of the Third Reich|''The Rise and Fall of the Third Reich'']] in the context of its use in the [[Wikipedia:Kriegsmarine|German Navy]].<ref name="Annotation 13">{{Facebook|username=starwarsbooks|url=posts/199642040090838|name=Star Wars Books|text=HEIR annotation #13|archivedate=20120922151830}}</ref> The rank was introduced into the modern [[canon]] continuity by the novel ''[[Aftermath]]''<ref name="Aftermath" /> and was first pictured through Thrawn's return to canon in ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="Steps Into Shadow" />

